  "result": "`npm test` passes now: all 243 tests. I fixed two bugs in `src/` and didn't touch the tests.\n\n1. **Tax was charged before the discount** (`src/cart.js`). `total()` added tax to the subtotal and then took the discount off. The comment in the code and the tests both say the discount comes off the pre-tax subtotal first, and tax is charged on what's left. I swapped the order, so a $100 cart with $20 off and 10% tax now comes to $88 instead of $90.\n2. **A fixed discount could push the total below zero** (`src/discount.js`). A $20 discount on a $5 item gave −$14.50. The discount now stops at zero.\n\nPercentage discounts didn't need a fix: with values from 0 to 100% they can never go below zero.",
